# Paths waived for the CONTENT scan in .githooks/pre-commit and pre-push.
#
# One glob per line, with the reason beside it. This waives CONTENT only:
# the committer's identity, the commit message and the FILE NAME are never
# exempted by anything in here, and the guard on those is unchanged.
#
# The file is committed on purpose. An exception recorded here is a decision
# somebody can review in a diff; an exception made with `--no-verify` is a
# decision nobody ever sees again.

# The AI enrichment feature (src/ai.js) calls the provider's official SDK, and
# package.json has to name that SDK in optionalDependencies for npm to install
# it. The name is the package's real identifier, not an attribution. Without
# this entry no commit could touch package.json at all, so every dependency
# bump at the root (sharp, mysql2, the SDK itself) was blocked. The lockfile
# is already skipped by the hook; package.json is the only path that needs it.
# Approved by the owner on 2026-10-16.
package.json
